/-!
# A symmetric-three factor of the original Thompson action

When the literal image of J(I₀) on V_I is solvable, B.2.5 supplies a
faithful action generated by best offenders. The proved solvable FF
classification constructs its internal S₃ factors. Applying A.1.31 to
their inverse image in the original SQTK group bounds the family by two;
no prime-rank bound is transported through an arbitrary quotient.

Select the whole image in the single-factor case and an actual coordinate
in the two-factor case. The selected S₃ is normal in the Thompson image
and subnormal in the original quotient. Every two-perfect actor preserves
it. Its normalizer is its product with its centralizer, with trivial
intersection, since every automorphism of S₃ is inner.

The application retains the same Y, I₀, reciprocal plane, lifted cubic
and faithful nine-group. Both L₁⁺ and the nine-group are proved to be
two-perfect and hence normalize the selected factor. Solvability is only
the branch condition: the nonsolvable A₅/L₃(2) selection and final cubic
projection contradiction remain open, as do the guarded same-G,T
specialization and the remaining source reductions through 14.7.52.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, proof of 14.7.32, printed pp.1058–1059,
using B.2.16 and A.1.31(1), refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/

